<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.5.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02156</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.5.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>0127790a-d791-4ea3-8d26-2b43524f8679</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para><emphasis><emphasis>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</emphasis></emphasis></para>
<para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<para>For questions 1 - 2, decide whether each statement is true or false.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x(x−5)=0\) has only one solution.</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> True </item>
  <item> False </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> False</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>A solution to \(x^2−49=0\) is \(x=-7\).</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> True </item>
  <item> False </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> True</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>Use graphing technology to determine the number of solutions for the equation \((x-4)(x+5)=−20\). Then find any solutions.</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> No solution </item>
  <item> One solution; \(x=1\) </item>
  <item> Two solutions; \(x=1\) and \(x=0\) </item>
  <item> Two solutions; \(x=-1\) and \(x=0\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Two solutions; \(x=-1\) and \(x=0\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>Use graphing technology to determine the number of solutions for the equation \((x+2)(x+5)=−2\). Then find any solutions.</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> No solution </item>
  <item> Two solutions; \(x=-3\) and \(x=4\) </item>
  <item> Two solutions; \(x=-3\) and \(x=-4\) </item>
  <item> Two solutions; \(x=3\) and \(x=4\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Two solutions; \(x=-3\) and \(x=-4\)</para>
<para>For questions 5 – 8, choose the best method to solve the equation and then use the method to find the solution.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(x(x−6)=0\)</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> \(x=0\) and \(x=-6\) </item>
  <item> \(x=6\) </item>
  <item> \(x=0\) and \(x=6\) </item>
  <item> \(x=6\) and \(x=-6\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x=0\) and \(x=6\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(\frac {1}{2}(x−4)^2=32\)</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> \(x=-4\) and \(x=4\) </item>
  <item> \(x=-12\) and \(x=4\) </item>
  <item> \(x=-8\) and \(x=8\) </item>
  <item> \(x=12\) and \(x=-4\) </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x=12\) and \(x=-4\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item>\((x+7)(x−2)=−8\)</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> \(x=-7\) and \(x=2\) </item>
  <item> \(x=-8\) and \(x=-1\) </item>
  <item> \(x=-6\) and \(x=1\) </item>
  <item> No solutions </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x=-6\) and \(x=1\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="8" type="enumerated">
  <item>\((x−4)(x+9)=−42.25\)</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> \(x=-2.5\) </item>
  <item> \(x=-3\) and \(x=-2\) </item>
  <item> \(x=-5\) and \(x=-1\) </item>
  <item> No solutions </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x=-2.5\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="9" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which statement is true of the equation \(x^2+36=0\)?</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> The solutions are \(x=0\) and \(x=6\). </item>
  <item> The solution is \(x=6\). </item>
  <item> The solutions are \(x=6\) and \(x=-6\). </item>
  <item> The equation has no solutions. </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> The equation has no solutions.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="10" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which statement is true of the equation \(x^2+9x=0\)?</item>
</list>
<list>
  <item> The solution is \(x=-9\). </item>
  <item> The solutions are \(x=0\) and \(x=-9\). </item>
  <item> The solutions are \(x=9\) and \(x=-9\). </item>
  <item> The equation has no solutions. </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> The solutions are \(x=0\) and \(x=-9\).</para></section>
